(1, 2, "Zamonaviy umumiy anesteziyaning komponentlarini belgilang.",
 ["Gipnoz (hushni o‘chirish)", "Analgeziya", "Qo‘zg‘alish bosqichini uzaytirish", "Nafas markazini tormozlash"],
 "Mark the components of modern general anaesthesia.",
 ["Hypnosis (loss of consciousness)", "Analgesia", "Prolonging the excitement stage", "Depression of the respiratory centre"],
 "Komponentlarga amneziya, miorelaksatsiya va noxush vegetativ reflekslarni to‘xtatish ham kiradi.",
 "The components also include amnesia, muscle relaxation and suppression of unwanted autonomic reflexes."),
(1, 2, "Vena ichiga yuboriladigan narkoz vositalarini belgilang.",
 ["Propofol", "Tiopental natriy", "Sevofluran", "Azot zakisi"],
 "Mark the intravenous anaesthetic agents.",
 ["Propofol", "Thiopental sodium", "Sevoflurane", "Nitrous oxide"],
 "Sevofluran va azot zakisi — ingalyatsion anestetiklar.",
 "Sevoflurane and nitrous oxide are inhalational anaesthetics."),
(1, 2, "Benzodiazepinlarni belgilang.",
 ["Diazepam", "Midazolam", "Buspiron", "Gidroksizin"],
 "Mark the benzodiazepines.",
 ["Diazepam", "Midazolam", "Buspirone", "Hydroxyzine"],
 "Buspiron — 5-HT1A qisman agonisti, gidroksizin — H₁-blokator; ikkalasi ham qaramlik chaqirmaydi.",
 "Buspirone is a 5-HT1A partial agonist and hydroxyzine an H₁ blocker; neither causes dependence."),
(2, 2, "Galotan (ftorotan) ning asosiy kamchiliklarini belgilang.",
 ["Miokardni katexolaminlarga sezgirlashtiradi — aritmiyalar", "Galotan gepatitini chaqirishi mumkin", "Nafas yo‘llarini kuchli qitiqlaydi", "Analgetik ta’siri juda kuchli"],
 "Mark the main drawbacks of halothane.",
 ["It sensitizes the myocardium to catecholamines, causing arrhythmias", "It can cause halothane hepatitis", "It strongly irritates the airways", "Its analgesic effect is very strong"],
 "Galotan hidi yoqimli va qitiqlamaydi; shu sababli u ilgari induksiyada ishlatilgan.",
 "Halothane has a pleasant, non-irritant smell, which is why it was once used for induction."),
(2, 2, "Propofolning nojo‘ya ta’sirlarini belgilang.",
 ["Gipotenziya", "Nafasning tormozlanishi", "Arterial gipertenziya", "Gallyutsinatsiyalar va qo‘rqinchli tushlar"],
 "Mark the side effects of propofol.",
 ["Hypotension", "Respiratory depression", "Arterial hypertension", "Hallucinations and frightening dreams"],
 "Gipertenziya va gallyutsinatsiyalar ketaminga xos.",
 "Hypertension and hallucinations are typical of ketamine."),
(2, 2, "Ketaminning qaysi ta’sirlari uning dala va shoshilinch sharoitda qulayligini belgilaydi?",
 ["AQB ni pasaytirmaydi", "Nafas va himoya reflekslari saqlanadi", "Kalla ichi bosimini pasaytiradi", "Uyg‘onish mutlaqo asoratsiz kechadi"],
 "Which effects of ketamine make it convenient in field and emergency conditions?",
 ["It does not lower blood pressure", "Breathing and protective reflexes are preserved", "It lowers intracranial pressure", "Recovery is completely free of complications"],
 "Ketamin kalla ichi va ko‘z ichi bosimini oshiradi, uyg‘onishda gallyutsinatsiyalar bo‘ladi.",
 "Ketamine raises intracranial and intraocular pressure, and hallucinations occur on recovery."),
(2, 2, "Benzodiazepinlarning asosiy ta’sirlarini belgilang.",
 ["Anksiolitik", "Talvasaga qarshi", "Antipsixotik", "Analgetik"],
 "Mark the main effects of benzodiazepines.",
 ["Anxiolytic", "Anticonvulsant", "Antipsychotic", "Analgesic"],
 "Ularning beshta ta’siri bor: anksiolitik, sedativ-uxlatuvchi, miorelaksant, talvasaga qarshi va amnestik; antipsixotik va analgetik ta’siri yo‘q.",
 "They have five effects: anxiolytic, sedative-hypnotic, muscle relaxant, anticonvulsant and amnestic; they are neither antipsychotic nor analgesic."),
(2, 2, "Giperprolaktinemiya (galaktoreya, amenoreya) neyroleptiklarning qaysi dofaminergik yo‘lga ta’siri bilan bog‘liq?",
 ["Tuberoinfundibulyar yo‘l", "Gipofiz orqali prolaktin sekretsiyasining tormozlanishi yo‘qoladi", "Nigrostriar yo‘l", "Mezolimbik yo‘l"],
 "Hyperprolactinaemia (galactorrhoea, amenorrhoea) is linked to the action of neuroleptics on which dopaminergic pathway?",
 ["The tuberoinfundibular pathway", "The dopaminergic inhibition of prolactin release through the pituitary is lost", "The nigrostriatal pathway", "The mesolimbic pathway"],
 "Nigrostriar yo‘l blokadasi ekstrapiramid buzilishlarga, mezolimbik yo‘l blokadasi antipsixotik ta’sirga olib keladi.",
 "Blockade of the nigrostriatal pathway causes extrapyramidal disorders, and of the mesolimbic pathway the antipsychotic effect."),
(3, 2, "Benzodiazepinlarni qo‘llashda qanday ehtiyot choralari zarur?",
 ["Kursni 2–4 haftadan oshirmaslik", "Opioidlar bilan birga qo‘llashdan saqlanish", "Dozani bir kunda keskin to‘xtatish", "Surunkali xavotirda birinchi tanlov sifatida uzoq buyurish"],
 "What precautions are needed when using benzodiazepines?",
 ["Keeping the course no longer than 2–4 weeks", "Avoiding combination with opioids", "Stopping the dose abruptly within one day", "Prescribing them long term as first choice in chronic anxiety"],
 "Uzoq qabul qilingan benzodiazepin asta-sekin kamaytiriladi; surunkali xavotirda birinchi tanlov — SSRI va psixoterapiya.",
 "Long-term benzodiazepines are tapered gradually; in chronic anxiety the first choice is an SSRI with psychotherapy."),
(3, 2, "Flumazenilni qo‘llashda qanday xavf bor?",
 ["Ta’siri qisqa bo‘lgani uchun qayta tormozlanish yuzaga kelishi mumkin", "Surunkali iste’molchilarda talvasa qo‘zg‘atishi mumkin", "Nafas markazini falajlashi mumkin", "Opioid zaharlanishini kuchaytiradi"],
 "What risks arise when flumazenil is used?",
 ["Its short action may allow re-sedation", "It may provoke seizures in chronic users", "It may paralyse the respiratory centre", "It worsens opioid poisoning"],
 "Trisiklik antidepressantlar bilan aralash zaharlanishda ham talvasa xavfi bor.",
 "There is also a risk of seizures in mixed poisoning with tricyclic antidepressants."),
